{"duration_api_ms":110462,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6638e88f-44d5-4c03-9aa5-f705d6ebd50f","total_cost_usd":1.282165,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":45268,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":33179,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":30044},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":45268,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":33179,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":45268,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":45268},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":33179,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":45268,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.282165,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":30044,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"RECEIPT sha=7535918bb3a6fb867bf8e4158d3984f2dbb62f929b72b07f6cc83e510c4e8ea3 end=PANEL-40b31d483fee92c3 nonce=ab5af02f2e87adf7\n\n**adversarial: needs-attention (6)**\n\n1. listview.cpp:868 — `self->m_hwnd = hwnd;` dereferences `self` before the `if (!self)` guard at listview.cpp:872. `cs->lpCreateParams` is null for any window created without passing `this`, and the class name `L\"ResoluteListView\"` (listview.cpp:89) is registered process-wide, so any `CreateWindowExW(0, L\"ResoluteListView\", ...)` from outside the class — or a `DialogBox`/resource-template instantiation of that class — null-derefs during WM_NCCREATE and kills the process.\n2. listview.cpp:907 — `self->m_columns[self->m_resizingCol].width = newW;` indexes with a stale index: `ClearColumns()` (listview.cpp:216) empties `m_columns` without resetting `m_resizingCol` or `m_sortCol`, and the resize drag holds mouse capture across that call, so a `ClearColumns()` during a drag turns the next WM_MOUSEMOVE into an out-of-bounds write on a `std::vector` of size 0.\n3. listview.cpp:986 — `HitTestScrollbar` (listview.cpp:352-357) tests only the geometric track and ignores `m_scrollbarVisible` and `m_scrollbarAlpha`, which OnPaint (listview.cpp:492) requires before drawing anything. With a single item and no visible scrollbar, any click within 4px of the client right edge sets `m_scrollbarDragging`, takes capture, and swallows the row selection; dragging then scrolls an unscrollable list.\n4. listview.cpp:139 — `GetDIBits` is called only when `ii.hbmColor` is non-null, but mask-only (1-bpp) icons have `hbmColor == nullptr`, leaving `pixels` all zero. The alpha probe at listview.cpp:149-152 then sets `hasAlpha = false`, listview.cpp:159 forces `a = 255`, and listview.cpp:177 permanently caches an opaque black square for that HICON.\n5. listview.cpp:111 — the cache is keyed on the raw `HICON` value and is never evicted per-entry (only wholesale at listview.cpp:104). Win32 recycles icon handles after `DestroyIcon`, so a caller that frees an icon and loads another receives the previous icon's bitmap for the new handle; hostile or merely churning shell-icon providers make the list render arbitrary stale imagery.\n6. listview.cpp:443-451 — `BlinkLoop::Start` re-arms itself from its own completion callback with a captured raw `ListView*`, and nothing in the file or header (no destructor, no WM_DESTROY/WM_NCDESTROY case in the switch at listview.cpp:874-1144) cancels it. Destroying a ListView while editing leaves a perpetual animation writing `m_cursorBlinkPhase` and calling `Repaint()` through a dangling pointer; the same use-after-free applies to every animation lambda capturing `this` (listview.cpp:247, 255, 268, 272, 290, 305, 935, 1130).\n\n**consistency: needs-attention (6)**\n\n1. listview.cpp:294 — two contradictory WM_COMMAND packings are used for the same parent contract: `MAKEWPARAM(IDC_LISTVIEW_SORT, 0)` here and `MAKEWPARAM(IDC_LISTVIEW_EDITED, 0)` at listview.cpp:462 put the notification constant in the control-id position with a zero notify code, while listview.cpp:1035, listview.cpp:1069, listview.cpp:1082 and listview.cpp:1091 put `m_id` in the id position and the notification constant in the notify-code position. No parent dispatcher can decode both.\n2. listview.cpp:207 — `SetItemCount` sets `m_scrollbarVisible = true` unconditionally, contradicting listview.cpp:189 where the same flag is derived from `TotalContentHeight() > h - ContentTop()`. After any `SetItemCount` a non-overflowing list paints a full-track thumb until the next `Resize`.\n3. listview.cpp:53 — `ColumnX` is defined and declared (listview.h:171) but called nowhere in the file; same for `TotalColumnsWidth` at listview.cpp:60 (listview.h:172) and `GridRows` at listview.cpp:73 (listview.h:177).\n4. listview.cpp:1110 — `ch == VK_RETURN || ch == VK_ESCAPE` is dead: VK_RETURN (0x0D) and VK_ESCAPE (0x1B) are both below 0x20 and already rejected by the `ch < 0x20` term on the same line.\n5. listview.cpp:587 — ellipsis trimming is installed only on the PaintDetails body format; the formats created at listview.cpp:512 (header labels), listview.cpp:675 (icon labels), listview.cpp:748 (list rows) and listview.cpp:815 (inline edit) set NO_WRAP without trimming, so overlong text in those four paths spills past its layout rect instead of truncating.\n6. listview.cpp:1108 — WM_CHAR gates on `m_editActive`, but the VK_UP and VK_DOWN handlers at listview.cpp:1077 and listview.cpp:1086 do not: pressing an arrow during an edit moves and animates the selection while the edit overlay stays pinned to `m_editItemIdx` (listview.cpp:635) and the pending text silently follows the old row.\n\n**integration: needs-attention (4)**\n\n1. listview.cpp:314 — `ScrollToItem` converts an item index with `RowHeight()`, as do `EnsureVisible` at listview.cpp:322-328 and the wheel step at listview.cpp:892, but LargeIcons/SmallIcons lay out on `CellHeight()` and `GridCols()` (listview.cpp:411, listview.cpp:38-39). In either icon mode these public entry points scroll to an offset unrelated to the requested item, and `EnsureVisible` called from listview.cpp:1080/listview.cpp:1089 can scroll the selection out of view rather than into it.\n2. listview.cpp:195 — `UpdateDpi` reassigns `m_dpi` and recomputes only `m_selHighlightY`; `m_scrollY` and `m_scrollTargetY` remain expressed in the old DPI's pixels and are never re-clamped against the new `MaxScrollY()`, and the render target is not resized. A DPI change therefore leaves the view scrolled to a wrong, possibly out-of-range offset that only a later `Resize` corrects.\n3. listview.cpp:1025 — the inline-edit path `hitRow == m_lastClickIdx && m_editClickTimer` is unreachable in practice. The class registers CS_DBLCLKS (listview.cpp:85), so a second click inside the system double-click time arrives as WM_LBUTTONDBLCLK, which kills the timer and clears `m_lastClickIdx` (listview.cpp:1066-1067); a second click after that window finds the 500ms timer from listview.cpp:1039 already expired and `m_lastClickIdx` reset by listview.cpp:1138. Click-to-rename never fires.\n4. listview.cpp:368 — `KillTimer(m_hwnd, m_scrollbarTimer)` is issued without zeroing `m_scrollbarTimer`, and the re-arm on listview.cpp:370 is skipped whenever hovered or dragging. The member then holds an id for a timer that no longer exists and that WM_TIMER (listview.cpp:1127) will never clear, so subsequent calls keep issuing `KillTimer` on a dead id and the state no longer reflects whether a hide is pending.\n\n**record: needs-attention (2)**\n\n1. listview.h:3 — the header comment claims \"virtual scrolling\" for the control as a whole, but `PaintIcons` iterates `for (int i = 0; i < m_itemCount; i++)` at listview.cpp:685, calling `GridCellRect` and the user `ItemProvider` (listview.cpp:703) for every item on every frame and merely `continue`-ing on the off-screen ones. Only Details (listview.cpp:577-580) and List (listview.cpp:754-757) compute a visible range; both icon modes are fully unvirtualized.\n2. listview.cpp:196 — the comment \"Recalculate DPI-dependent cached positions\" claims the DPI-dependent cached state is refreshed, but the body recalculates only `m_selHighlightY`. `m_scrollY`, `m_scrollTargetY` (listview.cpp:222 shows they are scroll-space values scaled by `RowHeight()`/`CellHeight()`) and any in-flight animation targets created at listview.cpp:255 and listview.cpp:305 are left at their old-DPI magnitudes.","ttft_ms":98648,"type":"result","duration_ms":110555,"uuid":"8b1b48bc-e84a-4586-8445-0f319bfc3482","ttft_stream_ms":1123,"time_to_request_ms":88,"first_content_frame_ms":1124,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
